  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION OF CRITICALLY ENDANGERED SUMATRAN TIGER, RHINO AND ELEPHANT POPULATIONS IN WAY KAMBAS NATIONAL PARK, SUMATRA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) ENSURE THE ONGOING OPERATION OF THE ELEPHANT RESPONSE UNIT (ERU) RIVER PATROL TO CONDUCT REGULAR PATROLS IN ORDER TO PREVENT ILLEGAL ACTIVITIES AND FOREST FIRES IN THE NORTHERN AND NORTHEASTERN AREAS OF WAY KAMBAS NATIONAL PARK (2) INCREASE EFFECTIVENESS OF THE ERU RIVER PATROL WORK BY UPGRADING THEIR FACILITIES, SUPPLIES, TOOLS, AND EQUIPMENT, SUCH AS A 4X4 TRUCK, NEEDED FOR THEIR WORK AND INCREASE THE NUMBER OF PATROL TEAM STAFF.</narrative>
  </description>
